From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: max77705: quiet the interrupt at shutdown

Shutdown opens the USB switch, which raises an interrupt, and leaves the
interrupt enabled. The I2C controller shuts down right after its
clients and marks its adapter suspended, so the regmap-irq thread then
transferred on a suspended adapter: "i2c i2c-9: Transfer while
suspended" and a WARN in __i2c_transfer on every reboot. Disable the
interrupt once the switch is open.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/mfd/max77705.c |    8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)


diff --git a/drivers/mfd/max77705.c b/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
index 4f381e4..99e4a99 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/max77705.c
@@ -243,6 +243,14 @@ static void max77705_i2c_shutdown(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 
 	if (max77705->regmap_muic)
 		max77705_usbc_set_switch(max77705->regmap_muic, MAX77705_USBC_SW_OPEN);
+
+	/*
+	 * Nothing may talk to the chip after this: the I2C controller is shut
+	 * down right after its clients and marks its adapter suspended, and an
+	 * interrupt (the switch change above raises one) would make the
+	 * regmap-irq thread transfer on it ("Transfer while suspended").
+	 */
+	disable_irq(i2c->irq);
 }
 
 static int max77705_suspend(struct device *dev)
